        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0804" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg682"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Palmer to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 21, 1889</date>.
                        (Received July 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 8, of the
                    27th instant, I have the honor to report that in the absence of a reply on the
                    part of the Spanish Government to a note of the legation of February 8, 1888,
                    presenting the claim for the return of tonnage dues illegally collected from the
                    American brig <hi rendition="#italic">J. W. Parker</hi>, I have addressed a note
                    of this date to the minister of state, requesting action on the case. As soon as
                    I receive his reply the entire correspondence will be forwarded to the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. W. Palmer.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
